  "title": "osf review run: lens-driven agent review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds `osf review run`, a new command that selects review lenses for a change, assembles a redacted context prompt, drives installed coding agents headless as reviewers, verifies their quoted findings against the files, reduces the answers to a per-lens and whole-review verdict, journals every answer and the decision, and can post the result to a pull request. Alongside it, the agent list in `agents.rs` becomes the single source of truth for the five agents osf can drive (dsh, omp, opencode, codex, claude), `osf.toml` gains `[agents]` and `[review]` tables, a new `scan-secret` rule redacts secrets from prompts and findings, and suppression markers gain rule ownership so a checker only reports its own unused markers. A new `review.yml` workflow runs the review from the base branch with the pull request's tree mounted read-only.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
